# Proprietary bug reports (GMV source snippets) — never commit.
# Repo-derived review reports (no proprietary content) are whitelisted
# explicitly, one line per file, so the default stays never-commit.
#
# Adding a file to this folder does NOTHING until it is listed here. That is
# the point (deny by default), but it fails silently: the file is simply absent
# from the commit, with no error. If a doc you wrote here is missing from a
# diff, check this list first.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
# The two below were committed before this whitelist existed. Tracked files are
# unaffected by .gitignore, so they persist either way; listed for honesty, so
# this file describes the folder's actual contents rather than a subset of them.
